        "original_id": "f0db3ed3-a42e-56db-a8ed-7f1fb6907f99",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Modern Music, Modern Records, Flair Records\n- People: the Bihari brothers, Little Richard, Etta James, Joe Houston, Ike Turner, Tina Turner, John Lee Hooker, Richard Wayne Penniman\n- Places: Los Angeles\n- Topics: R&B record labels, music industry\n\nFacts:\n- Modern Music was an American record company and label formed in 1945 in Los Angeles by the Bihari brothers.\n- Richard Wayne Penniman was born on December 5, 1932, and he became known as Little Richard.\n- Modern Records was one of the major R&B labels in the 1950s and 1960s, with artists including Etta James, Joe Houston, Little Richard, Ike and Tina Turner, and John Lee Hooker.\n- Little Richard was an American musician, singer, actor, comedian, and songwriter.\n- Flair Records was a subsidiary of Modern Records.",
